    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0536" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg526"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 19.</seg></opener>
                <head>The Duke of Newcastle to Lieutenant Governor Gordon.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Downing Street,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 17, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your despatch of the 18th
                    of January last, I have the honor to acquaint you that her Majesty’s government
                    consider that you exercised a wise discretion in allowing the accused persons in
                    the case of the steamer Chesapeake copies of the requisition and warrant to
                    which you refer.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>NEWCASTLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
